index 0000000..405a849
--- /dev/null
+++ b/IMPLEMENTER_REPORT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,67 @@
+IMPLEMENTER_REPORT:
+
+ROUND: 0
+STATUS: DONE
+
+SUGGESTION_RESOLUTIONS:
+none
+
+SELF_REVIEW:
+- AC1 — entry no longer exposes a directory-level resolution status or its reason strings:
+  `ExpectedSetEntry` no longer has a `resolution` field; `ResolutionStatus` now documents
+  and serves Skill files only. `generate_manifest` derives failure via
+  `ExpectedSetEntry::is_failed()` (any owned Skill file missing). `grep -rn "\.resolution"`
+  over `crates/`, `tests/`, and `validation/` shows only `SkillFile::resolution` reads
+  (skill-index `is_failed`/tests, validation-runner `validate_all`/tests, deploy
+  `dev.rs`/`pack.rs`, `tests/test_toolkit_setup.rs`); no `entry.resolution` remains.
+- AC2 — failure messages keep naming location and reason:
+  unchanged. `failed_entry` still places the directory/malformed-`skillPath` reason on
+  the owned root Skill file (`skill file not found: <path>`, `vendor skill directory not
+  found: <path>`, `upstream skill directory not found: <path>`, `malformed skillPath
+  "<path>"...`), and dev/pack/validation still format messages from those file-level
+  reasons (e.g. pack `'<name>' (root skill file, <path>): <reason>`, dev
+  `missing skill files, skipping: ...`, validation FAIL naming the file).
+- AC3 — compiles and tests green; no consumer reads the retired status:
+  `cargo test --workspace` → 334 passed, 0 failed (exit 0).
+  `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets` → exit 0, no clippy lints on the workspace.
+  Two pre-existing cargo warnings remain in `crates/validation/Cargo.toml` (unused
+  deps `anyhow`, `serde_json`); they are untouched by this task and are not clippy lints.
+  `rustfmt --check` passes for both edited Rust files (the wider repo has unrelated
+  pre-existing formatting drift, left untouched).
+- AC4 — behavior unchanged vs the previous ticket:
+  dev policy (warn+skip on failed entry), pack strictness (bail naming every missing
+  file before `generate_manifest` is called), tarball layout, installed layout, lock
+  format, and all entry-state verdicts are untouched — consumers already read Skill
+  files. `generate_manifest` skips exactly failed entries; pack calls it only after
+  `reject_failed_entries`, so shipped manifests are unchanged. `tests/test_install.rs`
+  (pack/tarball referee) 7/7 passed; `validation/run.rs` on the real tree → PASS.
+- AC5 — existing suites stay green without relaxing assertions:
+  `rust-script --test tests/test_install.rs` 7/7; `tests/test_toolkit_setup.rs` 1/1;
+  `tests/test_github_verify.rs` 27/27; `tests/test_check.rs` 8/8;
+  `validation/run.rs` (test mode) 0 tests/exit 0 and script mode PASS. In the
+  skill-index suite the removed entry-level assertions were replaced with equivalent or
+  stronger file-level assertions (`!is_failed()` + root Skill file `Resolved`; missing
+  entry reason still asserted on the root Skill file), not deleted.
+- No issues found. No out-of-scope changes (no dependency, layout, or lock-format edits).
+
+CHANGED_FILES:
+- crates/skill-index/src/lib.rs — removed the retired `ExpectedSetEntry::resolution`
+  field/reason strings; `ResolutionStatus` documented as file-level; `generate_manifest`
+  skips via `is_failed()`; discovery helpers no longer set the entry status; migrated
+  enumerator tests to Skill-file facts without weakening them.
+- crates/validation-runner/src/lib.rs — test fixture `test_entry` no longer sets the
+  retired field; still builds one resolved root Skill file.
+- CONTEXT.md — Expected-set entry definition no longer advertises directory-level
+  resolution; failed-entry derivation stays on the missing Skill file.
+- crates/deploy/src/dev.rs (pre-existing) — already reads `SkillFile::resolution`;
+  unchanged.
+- crates/deploy/src/pack.rs (pre-existing) — already reads `SkillFile::resolution` and
+  names every missing file; unchanged.
+- tests/test_toolkit_setup.rs (pre-existing) — already reads Skill-file facts; unchanged.
+- tests/test_install.rs (pre-existing) — packaging/tarball referee; unchanged.
+- docs/adr/0045-expected-set-entry-resolves-its-skill-files.md (pre-existing) — records
+  the retirement decision; unchanged.
+
+SUMMARY: Retired the entry-level resolution status so failed-entry derivation, dev/pack
+messages, and manifest filtering all use the Skill files the entry owns, with the full
+workspace and rust-script suites green.
